        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add local transcript bridge and coordination handoffs",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThis is a full rewrite of the original prototype on top of current `main`.\n\n- Adds an opt-in, local-only Claude Code transcript bridge at `GET /api/cc/transcript`.\n- Adds `/talk`, a responsive transcript/status surface with honest disabled, locked, empty, and live states.\n- Adds transport-neutral TypeScript SDK helpers for coordination envelopes and ClickClack message handoffs.\n- Updates OpenAPI, generated SDK types, embedded web assets, feature/API/SDK docs, e2e coverage, and the changelog.\n\nThanks @Arnarsson for the original direction and contribution.\n\n## Why the rewrite\n\nThe original branch proved the product idea, but tied it to one contributor machine and a remotely reachable development host. It also widened existing auth behavior, granted transcript access through a generic profile scope, returned local paths, changed the Vite proxy to a private port, and cited a non-running test as verification.\n\nThis rewrite keeps the useful idea while replacing those assumptions with an explicit local capability contract. Existing magic-link and profile authorization behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## Security and privacy contract\n\n| Boundary | Implementation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Disabled by default | No fallback path. `CLICKCLACK_CC_TRUTH_STATUS_PATH` and `CLICKCLACK_CC_TRANSCRIPT_TOKEN` must both be configured. |\n| Human-only | A valid human session is required; bot tokens are rejected. |\n| Loopback-only | Socket address, host, browser origin, and forwarding headers must all be local. Remote and forwarded requests fail closed. |\n| Reverse-proxy defense | A separate operator-held capability token is required in `X-ClickClack-Transcript-Token`, so a loopback proxy cannot turn an ordinary session into transcript access. |\n| Tab-scoped browser storage | `/talk` asks for the capability once per tab and keeps it in `sessionStorage`; it is sent only to the same-origin API. |\n| No path disclosure | Transcript filenames are removed from selected-session, session-list, and error responses. |\n| Bounded execution | Status helper: 5-second runtime, bounded stdout/stderr, bounded pipe wait. Transcript reader: regular files only, newest 16 MiB only, 8 MiB line, 256 KiB message, and 2 MiB response budgets. |\n| Hosted/self-hosted restraint | The product CTA appears only on loopback hostnames. Direct remote visits receive no transcript data. |\n\n## Transcript behavior\n\n- The configured Python helper is invoked as `python3 <path> --json`.\n- `cwd` requests exact normalized working-directory selection.\n- Otherwise selection prefers `truth_status=active`, API-busy, `api_busy_unverified`, idle, then the first reported session.\n- `limit` defaults to 20 and is capped at 200.\n- Parsing keeps only user/assistant text from the bounded file tail.\n- Metadata, compaction summaries, sidechains, tool blocks, attachments, oversized rows/messages, malformed JSON, and unknown row types are ignored.\n- A valid session with no readable text returns `messages: []`; it does not invent dialogue or fail with a misleading parse error.\n\n## `/talk` UI\n\n- Shows selected lane, session, working directory, visible-session count, last-output proof, and real transcript text.\n- Has explicit unconfigured, unauthorized, capability-locked, empty, and live states.\n- Includes a setup-guide link and never renders transcript paths.\n- Validated at desktop and 390 px mobile widths; overflow and headline sizing were corrected during review.\n\n## Coordination SDK\n\nThe SDK now exports:\n\n- `coordinationLanes`: `now`, `waiting`, `watch`, `park`.\n- `buildMessageEnvelope`: builds the canonical six-field coordination envelope and copies receipt inputs.\n- `buildCoordinationHandoff`: combines that envelope with stable ClickClack message/workspace/channel/thread/route metadata.\n\nThese helpers only build typed JSON. They do not read transcripts, send messages, persist memory, or choose a transport.\n\n## Documentation and contracts\n\n- New detailed setup/security/parser/failure guide: `docs/features/local-transcript.md`.\n- API overview and feature index updated.\n- SDK guide expanded with a complete handoff example and lane semantics.\n- OpenAPI and generated TypeScript declarations include the transcript endpoint and required capability header.\n- Changelog credits `@Arnarsson`.\n\n## Removed from the prototype\n\n- Hardcoded contributor filesystem defaults.\n- Private/Tailnet host assumptions and port-specific Vite proxy changes.\n- Magic-link authorization weakening.\n- Generic `profile:read` transcript access.\n- Raw transcript-path responses.\n- Fabricated UI dialogue and non-running verification commands.\n\n## Verification\n\nVerified locally at exact head `381ba4fef2d3a0d3f5ffa2a5e655ff64881d9eac`:\n\n- `pnpm check` — Go tests, web/SDK builds, root/workspace typechecks, lint, and formatting pass.\n- `pnpm coverage` — pass; total Go statement coverage 85.6%.\n- `pnpm test:e2e` — 42/42 Chromium tests pass, including tab-scoped capability unlock.\n- `pnpm docs:site` — documentation site builds.\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...` — clean.\n- `docker build -t clickclack:pr39 .` — production image builds.\n- Focused API tests cover human/bot/remote/capability boundaries, path sanitization, selection, empty state, metadata filtering, oversized rows/messages, bounded helper execution/output, bounded file tail, cancellation, and response budget.\n- Source-blind browser/API behavior validation covered configured, unconfigured, remote, `cwd`, `limit`, metadata omission, desktop, and mobile states.\n- Autoreview: clean after resolving all accepted parser, resource-bound, host-routing, reverse-proxy, and subprocess-lifecycle findings.\n\n## Review focus\n\n1. The capability-gated local security boundary in `cc_transcript.go`.\n2. Transcript projection and resource budgets.\n3. Separation between the local observation surface and transport-neutral coordination SDK helpers.\n4. `/talk` locked/live UX and the operator setup documentation.\n",
